Glyph theater — technique notes
================================

The character grid in js/glyph-ramp.mjs, js/phase-color.mjs, js/crab-field.mjs,
and js/glyph-stage.mjs is original code. No third-party renderer source is
vendored. The ideas below are well-known and were reimplemented here.

aalib (LGPL-2.0-or-later) and libcaca (WTFPL)
  Brightness-to-glyph ramps, and fg/bg pairs so a cell's perceived tone is
  ink coverage times foreground plus the rest times background.

chafa (LGPL-3.0-or-later)
  Picking among density, block, and braille sets: braille for sparse
  deep-sea specks, blocks for the craft hatch, a density ramp for the shell.

Acerola, "I Tried Turning a 3D Game into ASCII Art" (2023), public video essay
  Split edge from fill. The surface normal chooses a stroke glyph; the lit
  interior stays on the brightness ramp. No shader source was copied.

cool-retro-term (GPL-3.0)
  Only the idea of a faint glow on the glyph buffer in the encore. This is
  not a terminal emulator and does not include that project's shaders.

asciinema-player (GPL-3.0) and play.core / ertdfgcvb experiments
  A cell grid with its own foreground and background, advanced over time,
  rather than a bitmap of the picture. No player source is included.

Bayer 4×4 ordered dither
  Public-domain threshold matrix, used to keep ramp bands from posterizing.

Geryon himself is a signed-distance crab (shell, claws, legs, stalks, eyes)
lit from one direction and resampled into the grid each frame.
